# Text is checked out with LF on every machine. Git for Windows' default
# (core.autocrlf) writes CRLF, and the recipes, the checks and bash read a \r
# as part of the line: AGENTS.md grew by one byte a line on the gate (spec 020).
* text=auto eol=lf
# Notes from the projects and ticks from the scheduled agent meet in this file.
# Both add lines, so both are kept. Here only: a file whose lines are edited or
# removed in place, or whose entries run over several lines, loses text this way
# (measured, spec 011).
docs/backlog.md merge=union
# The gate appends its verdict here on cloud while a run may append its own
# line in a checkout of cloud (spec 017). Lines only, added at the end.
docs/routine-log.md merge=union
